"y"}],"measure":"st_region_geometry"}]}]}]}]}}]},"contract":"A road user moves clockwise about a region's reference point at the observation: seen from above in the world frame, in the sense opposite to the one in which the ontology counts a left turn as counter-clockwise, the component of its velocity (kin.velocity) perpendicular to the line from the region's reference point (st.region_geometry) to the road user's reference point (kin.position) points clockwise about the region's reference point, and that component's magnitude exceeds `tol`, a tolerance that names only the source's speed resolution. It is computed from the cross product c of the offset of the road user's reference point from the region's reference point with the velocity (the offset's first component times the velocity's second, minus the offset's second component times the velocity's first), negative for clockwise motion: the concept holds where c is negative and c times c exceeds tol times tol times the squared length of the offset. Not denoted: the direction the road user points, since a vehicle backing clockwise moves clockwise; motion toward or away from the reference point, such as entering or leaving; whether the road user occupies the region, which the caller states; the designated direction of any carrier.","definition":null,"id":"drv.motion.clockwise_about_region","kind":"formula","narrowings":[],"params":[{"name":"tol","unit":"metre_per_second"}],"residues":[],"supersedes":null}
